responding `TabPanel` the same `id`; React Aria uses that key to build their accessible relationship."},"1490":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-25","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#customization","content":"The component exposes state through data attributes:"},"1491":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-26","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#customization","content":"`Tabs`: `data-design=\"underline\"` or `data-design=\"manilla\"`."},"1492":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-27","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#customization","content":"`Tab`: `data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focus-visible`, and `data-disabled`."},"1493":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-28","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#customization","content":"`TabPanel`: `data-inert` when a force-mounted inactive panel is not interactive."},"1494":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-29","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#customization","content":"Use these attributes to extend styling without replacing the accessibility behavior supplied by React Aria Components. You can also use render props in `className` to style based on state (e.g., `className={({ isSelected }) => isSelected ? 'active' : ''}`)."},"1495":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-30","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#customization","content":"Use `TabList`'s `containerProps` to customize the outer tab list shell, such as increasing its width."},"1496":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-31","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#best-practices","content":"Use Tabs for peer panels on the same page and URL."},"1497":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-32","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","u